[[:db/retract 17592186180007 :question/answer-fields 17592186177711] [:db/retract 17592186180013 :question/answer-fields 17592186177747] [:db/retract 17592186180176 :question/answer-fields 17592186178600] [:db/retract 17592186180295 :question/answer-fields 17592186179314] {:db/id 17592186179729 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c8aeb24-90cc-5de9-a270-6cd27812a200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179734 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180007 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x-y)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=4t\\,i+(4-4t)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=4t,\\,y(t)=4-4t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-4t)\\,j \\\\  & =4\\,i+(-4)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,dx+(x-y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x-y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t+(4-4t))\\cdot 4+(4t-(4-4t))\\cdot (-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16t+16-16t-16t+16-16t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}32-32t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =32{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9bb65a0-9776-5bce-a475-1e502f4ca7a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9bb65a0-9776-5bce-a475-1e502f4ca7a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bb65a0-9776-5bce-a475-1e502f4ca7a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee463fff-4400-5fdd-a30d-2b00697809d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4d23f52-8e6e-5e44-9af4-4b175eff035c" "answer-5adc34ca-ff1e-5a7e-a58d-e5f402ec7226" "answer-0f99d644-a1ad-5b43-b8be-36588f2a8d57" "answer-82a266c0-edf7-5c04-bf6f-54846fdc04bf" "answer-ee463fff-4400-5fdd-a30d-2b00697809d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4d23f52-8e6e-5e44-9af4-4b175eff035c" :answer/id #uuid "d4d23f52-8e6e-5e44-9af4-4b175eff035c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5adc34ca-ff1e-5a7e-a58d-e5f402ec7226" :answer/id #uuid "5adc34ca-ff1e-5a7e-a58d-e5f402ec7226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{2}1+t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f99d644-a1ad-5b43-b8be-36588f2a8d57" :answer/id #uuid "0f99d644-a1ad-5b43-b8be-36588f2a8d57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16{\\int }_{0}^{2}2t-1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82a266c0-edf7-5c04-bf6f-54846fdc04bf" :answer/id #uuid "82a266c0-edf7-5c04-bf6f-54846fdc04bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32{\\int }_{0}^{1}1+t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee463fff-4400-5fdd-a30d-2b00697809d2" :answer/id #uuid "ee463fff-4400-5fdd-a30d-2b00697809d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180013 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=1,\\,y(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x+y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)\\cdot 0+(1+t)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}1+t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f274490-0e74-56cf-8700-86afd0ca19e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f274490-0e74-56cf-8700-86afd0ca19e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f274490-0e74-56cf-8700-86afd0ca19e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-965cf5f1-7747-53da-b55f-f89432ec4b05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-965cf5f1-7747-53da-b55f-f89432ec4b05" "answer-707c6361-9302-5d0e-9948-6d00df2a56db" "answer-355201fd-a87c-5acd-a773-040c3348da1d" "answer-a41bf204-b1a4-53a0-b0d0-dbf22f8c37f2" "answer-c32393e5-5f10-5c78-bd47-75d6d938a51b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-965cf5f1-7747-53da-b55f-f89432ec4b05" :answer/id #uuid "965cf5f1-7747-53da-b55f-f89432ec4b05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}1+t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-707c6361-9302-5d0e-9948-6d00df2a56db" :answer/id #uuid "707c6361-9302-5d0e-9948-6d00df2a56db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-355201fd-a87c-5acd-a773-040c3348da1d" :answer/id #uuid "355201fd-a87c-5acd-a773-040c3348da1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)+t+1\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a41bf204-b1a4-53a0-b0d0-dbf22f8c37f2" :answer/id #uuid "a41bf204-b1a4-53a0-b0d0-dbf22f8c37f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c32393e5-5f10-5c78-bd47-75d6d938a51b" :answer/id #uuid "c32393e5-5f10-5c78-bd47-75d6d938a51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}t+{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c8aeb24-90cc-5de9-a270-6cd27812a200" :question/id #uuid "9c8aeb24-90cc-5de9-a270-6cd27812a200" :question/math-academy-id "q-124867" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the line $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,4]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt{2}t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,z(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})+8{t}^{3}\\cdot (2)-4{t}^{2}\\cdot (2)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}16{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f678fd71-00e1-594a-91b3-8c9260903977"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f678fd71-00e1-594a-91b3-8c9260903977" :answer-field/id #uuid "f678fd71-00e1-594a-91b3-8c9260903977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2d59a8c-93ee-5534-b2f2-ae231427b12e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2d59a8c-93ee-5534-b2f2-ae231427b12e" "answer-7491be96-5601-5301-a5ca-7f7629fc7e2c" "answer-ccbb774b-4bad-5678-9592-475093dad980" "answer-5653a3c0-a432-54b1-bd34-3f7fd032cf28" "answer-207e611c-1715-5848-8636-a148354824ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2d59a8c-93ee-5534-b2f2-ae231427b12e" :answer/id #uuid "b2d59a8c-93ee-5534-b2f2-ae231427b12e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}16{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7491be96-5601-5301-a5ca-7f7629fc7e2c" :answer/id #uuid "7491be96-5601-5301-a5ca-7f7629fc7e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}3{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccbb774b-4bad-5678-9592-475093dad980" :answer/id #uuid "ccbb774b-4bad-5678-9592-475093dad980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}4{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5653a3c0-a432-54b1-bd34-3f7fd032cf28" :answer/id #uuid "5653a3c0-a432-54b1-bd34-3f7fd032cf28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}4{t}^{4}-6{t}^{2}+2\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-207e611c-1715-5848-8636-a148354824ca" :answer/id #uuid "207e611c-1715-5848-8636-a148354824ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}8{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+3t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180176 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ]?$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx+x\\,dy+{z}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+{t}^{2}\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{t}^{2}\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e33dea3-f3c2-5a02-9f0a-3fc23f07af84"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e33dea3-f3c2-5a02-9f0a-3fc23f07af84" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e33dea3-f3c2-5a02-9f0a-3fc23f07af84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fd1d323b-e5df-5e29-88d7-6527a8a633a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c8a1d3b-7cc7-56d2-8a0b-b470fcd35f75" "answer-fd1d323b-e5df-5e29-88d7-6527a8a633a6" "answer-901a2e65-5fa9-5165-ba1b-6642336cd921" "answer-407b1421-300f-5650-8cf7-dd126bc29f0b" "answer-b1d6414c-0388-584f-92ec-491360dc6f39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c8a1d3b-7cc7-56d2-8a0b-b470fcd35f75" :answer/id #uuid "8c8a1d3b-7cc7-56d2-8a0b-b470fcd35f75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1+{t}^{2}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd1d323b-e5df-5e29-88d7-6527a8a633a6" :answer/id #uuid "fd1d323b-e5df-5e29-88d7-6527a8a633a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+{t}^{2}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-901a2e65-5fa9-5165-ba1b-6642336cd921" :answer/id #uuid "901a2e65-5fa9-5165-ba1b-6642336cd921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-407b1421-300f-5650-8cf7-dd126bc29f0b" :answer/id #uuid "407b1421-300f-5650-8cf7-dd126bc29f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1d6414c-0388-584f-92ec-491360dc6f39" :answer/id #uuid "b1d6414c-0388-584f-92ec-491360dc6f39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180295 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the helix $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z(t)=t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}-y\\,dx+x\\,dy+z\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\cdot 1\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1+t\\,dt \\\\  & =(t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi +\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi (1+\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a11798a-13e6-56d1-93c3-1b2f2fdacf74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a11798a-13e6-56d1-93c3-1b2f2fdacf74" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a11798a-13e6-56d1-93c3-1b2f2fdacf74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ee67649-cfe6-55fe-8d15-2b91a6e5a085" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6b321de-ff7e-5fef-afd8-96961b2c148e" "answer-5b212ba5-4523-505f-abd1-6ed94aa4f312" "answer-9ee67649-cfe6-55fe-8d15-2b91a6e5a085" "answer-41ad462e-980a-55e7-8603-ff255c0b0f91" "answer-95804867-920f-57f6-9af2-84579578a567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6b321de-ff7e-5fef-afd8-96961b2c148e" :answer/id #uuid "a6b321de-ff7e-5fef-afd8-96961b2c148e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b212ba5-4523-505f-abd1-6ed94aa4f312" :answer/id #uuid "5b212ba5-4523-505f-abd1-6ed94aa4f312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ee67649-cfe6-55fe-8d15-2b91a6e5a085" :answer/id #uuid "9ee67649-cfe6-55fe-8d15-2b91a6e5a085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi (1+\\pi )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ad462e-980a-55e7-8603-ff255c0b0f91" :answer/id #uuid "41ad462e-980a-55e7-8603-ff255c0b0f91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi (1-\\pi )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95804867-920f-57f6-9af2-84579578a567" :answer/id #uuid "95804867-920f-57f6-9af2-84579578a567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi (2+\\pi )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be" :question/id #uuid "7e1c746b-98be-5a3b-93f3-3c945fad75be" :question/math-academy-id "q-90723" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is a portion of the parabola parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(4t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=4t-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+4t-1)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2}-2t+4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{4}+4(2)^{3}-{2}^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[24+32-4] \\\\  & =52\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-516d65af-e99b-58a7-afb3-db833a18796f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-516d65af-e99b-58a7-afb3-db833a18796f" :answer-field/id #uuid "516d65af-e99b-58a7-afb3-db833a18796f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cf6010e-a80e-5fc9-aa97-fc8be288477c" "answer-d33fa25d-bc45-54e8-8056-40b5e874ab27" "answer-874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" "answer-7acff49a-3d77-5139-87b8-23f8a83a61d7" "answer-3ea3a4f2-a959-540f-86d2-a526fb567a9f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cf6010e-a80e-5fc9-aa97-fc8be288477c" :answer/id #uuid "6cf6010e-a80e-5fc9-aa97-fc8be288477c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d33fa25d-bc45-54e8-8056-40b5e874ab27" :answer/id #uuid "d33fa25d-bc45-54e8-8056-40b5e874ab27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" :answer/id #uuid "874aecd7-c4bb-5970-a264-ff44eec6444f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7acff49a-3d77-5139-87b8-23f8a83a61d7" :answer/id #uuid "7acff49a-3d77-5139-87b8-23f8a83a61d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ea3a4f2-a959-540f-86d2-a526fb567a9f" :answer/id #uuid "3ea3a4f2-a959-540f-86d2-a526fb567a9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180681 :tutorial/content "Line integrals with respect to $x$ and $y$ often come in pairs. For example, \n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C (x+y) \\, \\textrm dx + \\int\\limits_C (x-y) \\, \\textrm dy.\n$$\n\nWe usually express a sum of line integrals with respect to $x$ and $y$ as a single integral. In the case above, we can write this sum as\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C (x+y) \\, \\textrm dx + (x-y) \\, \\textrm dy.\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate this integral in this case where $C$ is given by the line segment\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\underbrace{(6t+1)}_{x(t)} \\,\\mathbf{i} + \\underbrace{(2t+1)}_{y(t)} \\,\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad t\\in\\left[0,1\\right].\n$$\n\nAlong the path $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx = 6t+1, \\qquad y = 2t+1.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+1)\\,j \\\\  & =6\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the line integral by applying a change of variables, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(x-y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+(x-y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x-y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t+1+2t+1)\\cdot 6+(6t+1-(2t+1))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+2)\\cdot 6+(4t)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}48t+12+8t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}56t+12\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={28{t}^{2}+12t|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =28+12 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179858 :activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
